1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,114
May 2, 2021.

2
00:00:02,114 --> 00:00:06,199
Early morning, off Point Loma, in San Diego.

3
00:00:06,199 --> 00:00:09,448
A 40-foot boat has lost its engine.

4
00:00:09,898 --> 00:00:12,968
32 passengers are on board, including three

5
00:00:12,968 --> 00:00:14,468
unaccompanied minors.

6
00:00:14,468 --> 00:00:16,895
They were told to stay below deck.

7
00:00:17,345 --> 00:00:19,956
In rain and large swells, the boat drifts

8
00:00:19,956 --> 00:00:21,612
aground, and breaks apart.

9
00:00:22,062 --> 00:00:23,249
Three people die.

10
00:00:23,249 --> 00:00:25,275
29 are pulled from the water.

11
00:00:25,275 --> 00:00:27,161
The captain swims to shore.

12
00:00:27,611 --> 00:00:30,539
The passengers had agreed to pay $15,000 to

13
00:00:30,539 --> 00:00:31,425
$18,000 each.

14
00:00:31,425 --> 00:00:33,945
Who sells a seat on a boat like that?

15
00:00:33,945 --> 00:00:36,805
And who is out there, trying to stop them?

16
00:00:37,405 --> 00:00:39,752
This is the case of human smuggling at sea.

17
00:00:42,352 --> 00:00:45,142
To understand the boats, start with the water

18
00:00:45,142 --> 00:00:46,320
south of San Diego.

19
00:00:46,770 --> 00:00:50,008
ICE describes the boats smugglers use there in

20
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:50,642
two ways.

21
00:00:50,642 --> 00:00:51,698
Pleasure craft.

22
00:00:51,698 --> 00:00:55,007
And pangas, repurposed Mexican fishing vessels.

23
00:00:55,007 --> 00:00:58,034
Long, open boats, sitting low in the water.

24
00:00:58,484 --> 00:01:01,738
In one case in April, 2022, CBP's Air and

25
00:01:01,738 --> 00:01:05,231
Marine Operations detected three pangas with

26
00:01:05,231 --> 00:01:08,802
their lights off, heading toward the maritime

27
00:01:08,802 --> 00:01:09,358
border.

28
00:01:09,358 --> 00:01:11,263
72 people were on board.

29
00:01:11,713 --> 00:01:14,524
The boats leave from the coast of Baja

30
00:01:14,524 --> 00:01:17,927
California, from places like Popotla, south of

31
00:01:17,927 --> 00:01:18,519
Tijuana.

32
00:01:18,519 --> 00:01:21,256
Many try to land in San Diego County.

33
00:01:21,256 --> 00:01:23,254
Some go much farther north.

34
00:01:23,704 --> 00:01:27,247
In July 2021 alone, the task force responded

35
00:01:27,247 --> 00:01:30,952
to 12 smuggling events off Orange, Los Angeles

36
00:01:30,952 --> 00:01:32,643
and Ventura counties.

37
00:01:33,093 --> 00:01:34,094
Some make it.

38
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:37,560
In August 2017, a Coast Guard camera followed

39
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:38,330
two boats.

40
00:01:38,330 --> 00:01:42,258
One landed at Point Loma, the other in Mission Bay.

41
00:01:42,258 --> 00:01:45,569
12 Mexican nationals were taken into Border

42
00:01:45,569 --> 00:01:46,725
Patrol custody.

43
00:01:47,175 --> 00:01:51,399
In San Diego Sector, from October 2020 to the

44
00:01:51,399 --> 00:01:54,872
end of August 2021, the Border Patrol

45
00:01:54,872 --> 00:01:59,002
intercepted 330 maritime-related events, and

46
00:01:59,002 --> 00:02:00,785
made 1,751 arrests.

47
00:02:01,235 --> 00:02:04,745
To fight back, the agencies built a joint command.

48
00:02:04,745 --> 00:02:07,763
The Regional Coordinating Mechanism. ReCoM.

49
00:02:08,213 --> 00:02:10,853
They share intelligence, pool their boats and

50
00:02:10,853 --> 00:02:13,141
aircraft, and plan operations together.

51
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:16,182
The head of the Border Patrol's San Diego

52
00:02:16,182 --> 00:02:18,583
Sector, Aaron Heitke, put it this way.

53
00:02:19,583 --> 00:02:21,055
Back to Point Loma.

54
00:02:21,505 --> 00:02:24,878
The captain that morning was Antonio Hurtado,

55
00:02:24,878 --> 00:02:27,351
a 40-year-old man from San Diego.

56
00:02:27,801 --> 00:02:30,694
According to his plea agreement, he repeatedly

57
00:02:30,694 --> 00:02:33,398
used controlled substances during the trip,

58
00:02:33,398 --> 00:02:35,726
and lost consciousness at least once.

59
00:02:35,726 --> 00:02:38,745
For more than an hour, the boat went in circles.

60
00:02:39,195 --> 00:02:42,522
Then, around six in the morning, the engine failed.

61
00:02:42,522 --> 00:02:45,262
The boat drifted toward the rocks near the

62
00:02:45,262 --> 00:02:47,024
Cabrillo National Monument.

63
00:02:47,474 --> 00:02:50,461
Hurtado jumped overboard, and swam to shore.

64
00:02:50,911 --> 00:02:52,850
29 people were rescued.

65
00:02:52,850 --> 00:02:54,704
Three did not survive.

66
00:02:54,704 --> 00:02:56,980
Maricela Hernandez-Sanchez.

67
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:58,919
Victor Perez-Degollado.

68
00:02:58,919 --> 00:03:01,364
Maria Eugenia Chavez-Segovia.

69
00:03:02,164 --> 00:03:04,945
In April 2022, Hurtado pleaded guilty.

70
00:03:04,945 --> 00:03:07,872
Three counts of attempted bringing in of

71
00:03:07,872 --> 00:03:09,994
migrants, resulting in death.

72
00:03:09,994 --> 00:03:13,360
He also admitted assaulting a federal officer.

73
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:16,799
He had kneed a Border Patrol agent in the head.

74
00:03:17,249 --> 00:03:20,347
That August, Judge Janis Sammartino sentenced

75
00:03:20,347 --> 00:03:22,689
him to 18 years in federal prison.

76
00:03:23,139 --> 00:03:25,406
She said it was the most serious kind of case

77
00:03:25,406 --> 00:03:26,061
she had seen.

78
00:03:26,511 --> 00:03:28,037
At sentencing, the U.S.

79
00:03:28,037 --> 00:03:31,023
attorney, Randy Grossman, said the passengers

80
00:03:31,023 --> 00:03:34,008
had put their savings and their lives in this

81
00:03:34,008 --> 00:03:35,203
defendant's hands.

82
00:03:35,203 --> 00:03:38,055
When Hurtado pleaded guilty, his advice had

83
00:03:38,055 --> 00:03:39,183
been three words.

84
00:03:39,633 --> 00:03:42,722
The head of HSI in San Diego, Chad Plantz,

85
00:03:42,722 --> 00:03:46,105
said the case showed that human smugglers have

86
00:03:46,105 --> 00:03:48,017
no respect for human life.

87
00:03:49,017 --> 00:03:50,788
Point Loma was not the last.

88
00:03:51,238 --> 00:03:52,752
November 26, 2022.

89
00:03:52,752 --> 00:03:55,863
Off Imperial Beach, a boat carrying 8

90
00:03:55,863 --> 00:03:58,470
migrants, and its two captains.

91
00:03:58,470 --> 00:03:59,899
Three people die.

92
00:04:00,349 --> 00:04:03,160
Prosecutors said the passengers had been told

93
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:04,972
to take off their life vests.

94
00:04:04,972 --> 00:04:07,720
A common practice, they wrote, so passengers

95
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:09,907
are quicker and more inconspicuous.

96
00:04:10,357 --> 00:04:14,044
The captain, Jorge Armando Preciado-Vasquez,

97
00:04:14,044 --> 00:04:16,307
was sentenced to 54 months.

98
00:04:16,307 --> 00:04:20,079
His co-captain, Alexis Martinez-Preciado, got

99
00:04:20,079 --> 00:04:20,917
50 months.

100
00:04:21,367 --> 00:04:23,079
Then, March 11, 2023.

101
00:04:23,079 --> 00:04:26,585
Close to midnight, in heavy fog, two pangas

102
00:04:26,585 --> 00:04:29,601
approach Black's Beach, in San Diego.

103
00:04:30,051 --> 00:04:32,220
The pangas overturn in the surf.

104
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:33,373
Eight people die.

105
00:04:33,373 --> 00:04:36,490
San Diego's fire chief, James Gartland, called

106
00:04:36,490 --> 00:04:39,066
it one of the worst maritime smuggling

107
00:04:39,066 --> 00:04:41,913
tragedies he could think of in California.

108
00:04:42,363 --> 00:04:44,999
A CBP spokesman blamed callous human

109
00:04:44,999 --> 00:04:48,293
smugglers, who have no regard for human life.

110
00:04:48,743 --> 00:04:50,910
The deaths had been climbing.

111
00:04:50,910 --> 00:04:54,123
Off Southern California, maritime smuggling

112
00:04:54,123 --> 00:04:56,962
deaths went from three in fiscal 2019,

113
00:04:56,962 --> 00:05:00,399
according to the regional task force, to 13 by

114
00:05:00,399 --> 00:05:03,312
late March of fiscal 2023, according to

115
00:05:03,312 --> 00:05:05,703
authorities cited by inewsource.

116
00:05:06,153 --> 00:05:09,643
And on May 5, 2025, a 20-foot panga from

117
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:13,307
Popotla, with 19 people on board, capsized

118
00:05:13,307 --> 00:05:16,709
about 200 yards off Del Mar. Four died.

119
00:05:16,709 --> 00:05:20,809
Two of them were children, 14 and 10 years old.

120
00:05:21,259 --> 00:05:24,692
Survivors said the captains told them to take

121
00:05:24,692 --> 00:05:26,446
off their life jackets.

122
00:05:26,446 --> 00:05:29,040
Each passenger paid about $13,500.

123
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:32,625
In April 2026, the two captains pleaded guilty.

124
00:05:32,625 --> 00:05:35,981
They were scheduled to be sentenced in June.

125
00:05:35,981 --> 00:05:39,414
We found no public record of their sentences.

126
00:05:39,864 --> 00:05:42,677
Three other people tied to the case were

127
00:05:42,677 --> 00:05:45,701
sentenced in federal court in San Diego, to

128
00:05:45,701 --> 00:05:47,459
between 10 and 21 months.

129
00:05:48,459 --> 00:05:51,117
On the other side of the country, the crossing

130
00:05:51,117 --> 00:05:51,753
is shorter.

131
00:05:51,753 --> 00:05:53,024
And just as dangerous.

132
00:05:53,474 --> 00:05:56,471
Saturday night, January 22, 2022.

133
00:05:56,471 --> 00:06:00,559
A 25-foot boat leaves Bimini, in the Bahamas,

134
00:06:00,559 --> 00:06:02,285
headed for Florida.

135
00:06:02,735 --> 00:06:05,606
On Sunday, in severe weather, it capsizes.

136
00:06:05,606 --> 00:06:08,409
No one on board is wearing a life jacket.

137
00:06:08,859 --> 00:06:12,288
On Tuesday morning, a good Samaritan rescues a

138
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:15,419
man from the capsized boat, about 45 miles

139
00:06:15,419 --> 00:06:17,357
east of Fort Pierce Inlet.

140
00:06:17,357 --> 00:06:20,711
He tells the Coast Guard 39 other people were

141
00:06:20,711 --> 00:06:21,382
with him.

142
00:06:21,832 --> 00:06:25,378
He was Juan Esteban Montoya, 22, from Colombia.

143
00:06:25,378 --> 00:06:27,491
His sister was on that boat.

144
00:06:27,491 --> 00:06:29,000
She did not survive.

145
00:06:29,450 --> 00:06:33,096
Crews searched more than 10,500 square miles.

146
00:06:33,096 --> 00:06:35,284
Five bodies were recovered.

147
00:06:35,284 --> 00:06:37,471
34 people were never found.

148
00:06:37,921 --> 00:06:41,120
On January 27, the commander of Coast Guard

149
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:43,724
Sector Miami called off the search.

150
00:06:44,174 --> 00:06:47,604
In March 2024, federal prosecutors in Miami

151
00:06:47,604 --> 00:06:51,273
unsealed an indictment against a Bahamian man,

152
00:06:51,273 --> 00:06:53,027
Vandrick Nelson Smith.

153
00:06:53,477 --> 00:06:56,121
He is charged with attempting to bring

154
00:06:56,121 --> 00:06:59,253
noncitizens into the United States, resulting

155
00:06:59,253 --> 00:07:01,062
in death, for that voyage.

156
00:07:01,062 --> 00:07:02,593
These are allegations.

157
00:07:02,593 --> 00:07:05,724
He is presumed innocent unless proven guilty.

158
00:07:05,724 --> 00:07:08,646
As of early 2025, his extradition case was

159
00:07:08,646 --> 00:07:10,664
still pending in the Bahamas.

160
00:07:10,664 --> 00:07:12,891
We found no later public update.

161
00:07:13,341 --> 00:07:13,884
The U.S.

162
00:07:13,884 --> 00:07:16,739
attorney in Miami, Markenzy Lapointe, said

163
00:07:16,739 --> 00:07:19,865
human smuggling ventures put people's lives at

164
00:07:19,865 --> 00:07:21,767
risk for the sake of profit.

165
00:07:22,217 --> 00:07:24,963
The Bimini route has a long history.

166
00:07:24,963 --> 00:07:28,470
In October 2013, a boat capsized about 7 miles

167
00:07:28,470 --> 00:07:29,233
off Miami.

168
00:07:29,233 --> 00:07:31,292
Four Haitian women drowned.

169
00:07:31,292 --> 00:07:34,647
The smuggler, Naaman Davis, from Bimini, had

170
00:07:34,647 --> 00:07:37,926
been smoking crack cocaine during the trip.

171
00:07:37,926 --> 00:07:40,137
He was sentenced to 14 years.

172
00:07:41,137 --> 00:07:43,121
The third front is in the Caribbean.

173
00:07:43,571 --> 00:07:46,781
Between the Dominican Republic and Puerto Rico

174
00:07:46,781 --> 00:07:48,317
lies the Mona Passage.

175
00:07:48,317 --> 00:07:51,806
Overloaded boats cross it, headed for Puerto Rico.

176
00:07:52,256 --> 00:07:55,772
In October 2026, a Coast Guard helicopter crew

177
00:07:55,772 --> 00:07:56,995
filmed this one.

178
00:07:56,995 --> 00:07:58,447
63 people on board.

179
00:07:58,447 --> 00:08:01,886
They were sent back to the Dominican Republic

180
00:08:01,886 --> 00:08:02,880
the next day.

181
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:06,017
In May 2026, a CBP aircraft out of

182
00:08:06,017 --> 00:08:09,652
Jacksonville found another one, near the Turks

183
00:08:09,652 --> 00:08:12,101
and Caicos Islands. 240 people.

184
00:08:12,101 --> 00:08:15,657
Its engines had lost power, and it was taking

185
00:08:15,657 --> 00:08:16,368
on water.

186
00:08:16,368 --> 00:08:18,818
Local authorities rescued them.

187
00:08:19,268 --> 00:08:21,212
Some boats don't make it.

188
00:08:21,212 --> 00:08:24,166
In May 2022, a boat from the Dominican

189
00:08:24,166 --> 00:08:27,743
Republic carried 48 people toward Puerto Rico.

190
00:08:27,743 --> 00:08:28,676
Eleven died.

191
00:08:29,126 --> 00:08:32,228
A Dominican man, Fermin Montilla, pleaded

192
00:08:32,228 --> 00:08:34,800
guilty to bringing in aliens at an

193
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:37,750
unauthorized place, resulting in death.

194
00:08:37,750 --> 00:08:41,457
In February 2025, he was sentenced to nine years.

195
00:08:41,907 --> 00:08:44,595
The head of HSI in San Juan, Rebecca

196
00:08:44,595 --> 00:08:47,581
Gonzalez-Ramos, had a warning for anyone

197
00:08:47,581 --> 00:08:49,672
thinking of making the trip.

198
00:08:50,122 --> 00:08:52,225
And the landings continue.

199
00:08:52,225 --> 00:08:55,946
On July 20, 2026, agents stopped two smuggling

200
00:08:55,946 --> 00:08:59,262
ventures on opposite ends of Puerto Rico.

201
00:08:59,262 --> 00:09:03,064
37 people were apprehended, along with one U.S.

202
00:09:03,064 --> 00:09:03,711
citizen.

203
00:09:04,711 --> 00:09:07,292
So what does the law say about the people who

204
00:09:07,292 --> 00:09:08,210
run these boats?

205
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:12,065
Under federal law, bringing someone into the U.S.

206
00:09:12,065 --> 00:09:15,262
anywhere other than a port of entry carries up

207
00:09:15,262 --> 00:09:16,860
to ten years in prison.

208
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:19,709
If lives are put in danger, up to twenty.

209
00:09:19,709 --> 00:09:22,697
If someone dies, up to life, or even death.

210
00:09:23,147 --> 00:09:25,859
And any vessel used in the crime is seized,

211
00:09:25,859 --> 00:09:27,499
and subject to forfeiture.

212
00:09:27,949 --> 00:09:30,567
Smuggling for profit can also bring a

213
00:09:30,567 --> 00:09:31,840
mandatory minimum.

214
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:34,811
Three years for each person, on a first or

215
00:09:34,811 --> 00:09:36,013
second violation.

216
00:09:36,463 --> 00:09:39,652
To find the boats before they land, CBP flies

217
00:09:39,652 --> 00:09:42,416
long-range patrols, looking for vessels

218
00:09:42,416 --> 00:09:44,826
heading north from Mexican waters.

219
00:09:45,276 --> 00:09:48,851
In May 2026, near Freeport, in the Bahamas, a

220
00:09:48,851 --> 00:09:52,584
CBP aircrew spotted a suspicious cabin cruiser.

221
00:09:52,584 --> 00:09:56,159
After hours of surveillance, two marine units

222
00:09:56,159 --> 00:09:56,874
moved in.

223
00:09:56,874 --> 00:09:58,780
21 people were on board.

224
00:09:59,230 --> 00:10:03,072
In September, near Angelfish Creek in Florida,

225
00:10:03,072 --> 00:10:07,082
a CBP aircraft on patrol spotted a 27-foot boat.

226
00:10:07,082 --> 00:10:10,089
One suspected smuggler. 22 migrants.

227
00:10:10,539 --> 00:10:14,337
Back in California, in January 2025, the Coast

228
00:10:14,337 --> 00:10:17,641
Guard cutter Terrell Horne and CBP crews

229
00:10:17,641 --> 00:10:21,357
stopped a boat about 20 miles off Point Loma.

230
00:10:21,357 --> 00:10:23,339
14 people were on board.

231
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:26,685
Off the Florida Keys, Coast Guard and CBP

232
00:10:26,685 --> 00:10:29,723
crews pull alongside makeshift vessels like

233
00:10:29,723 --> 00:10:32,407
this one, and take the passengers off.

234
00:10:32,857 --> 00:10:36,078
A CBP Air and Marine Operations official in

235
00:10:36,078 --> 00:10:39,748
San Diego, Brandon Tucker, summed up the problem.

236
00:10:40,748 --> 00:10:41,541
Point Loma.

237
00:10:41,541 --> 00:10:42,623
Imperial Beach.

238
00:10:42,623 --> 00:10:45,218
Black's Beach. Del Mar. Fort Pierce.

239
00:10:45,218 --> 00:10:46,444
The Mona Passage.

240
00:10:46,894 --> 00:10:49,525
$15,000. $18,000. $13,500.

241
00:10:49,525 --> 00:10:53,978
That's what a seat costs, according to court

242
00:10:53,978 --> 00:10:54,787
records.

243
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:56,946
The smugglers set the price.

244
00:10:56,946 --> 00:10:58,777
The passengers carry the risk.

245
00:10:58,777 --> 00:11:01,402
And the crews on the water keep looking for

246
00:11:01,402 --> 00:11:02,256
the next boat.

247
00:11:03,056 --> 00:11:05,045
Case file 007. Closed.

248
00:11:05,045 --> 00:11:08,389
The next file is already on the desk.
